yoyo commit now exits 1 when no commit happened, and 0 when one did. It's committed as f96bb6fc.

Before the fix, I built the binary and reproduced the problem in temp dirs. All four of these cases exited 0:
• a repo with no author identity
• outside a repo, with a message
• `-a` outside a repo
• a failed --amend

After the fix, the same four commands print the same text and exit 1.

What changed (`src/commands_git.rs`):
• Every arm where the git commit fails now returns 1. That covers the message path, both prompted paths (accept the suggestion, or edit it), and a failure in -a staging.
• `handle_commit_amend now returns a status, and handle_commit_status` passes it up.
• The doc comment above handle_commit_status said "0 otherwise", which is no longer true, so I rewrote it.
• `dispatch_sub.rs needed no change: the commit arm already goes through exit_if_nonzero`.

Exit-code rule: yoyo mirrors git's own exit status. "Nothing to commit" (git exits 1) and -a with nothing staged now exit 1. Three cases still exit 0 on purpose:
• a successful commit or amend
• bare `yoyo commit` with nothing staged, which only prints a hint and never runs git commit (an existing test already pins this)
• a declined prompt

Tests: these are in tests/integration.rs, not in-process function calls as the task asked. The commit path writes a risk snapshot into the current directory on success and calls git there, so a test inside the crate would touch the real repo. Running the built binary in temp dirs avoids that and checks the exact exit code a user sees; earlier #982 fixes test the same way. I made git's identity fully controlled (user.useConfigOnly=true, no system or global config), so the no-identity case can't accidentally pass by picking up the host's identity. Cases covered:
• five failure cases that must exit 1, each also checking the expected error text appears
• a successful commit that must exit 0, with git log confirming the commit exists
• amend in both directions

I ran two positive controls one at a time, each as a single break → test → restore command. Each failed the right test by name and went green after the restore. No sabotage markers are left in the code.

Checks: build, the full test suite, clippy with -D warnings, and fmt --check all pass. I also added a sentence about commit's exit codes to docs/src/usage/commands.md.

Issue #982: I edited the body and read it back with gh issue view 982. commit (f96bb6fc) is now in the "Already fixed" list, and config <unknown> is in the "Known still exit 0" list. The commit message says "Part of #982", since bare run, index <path> and config <unknown> are still open.

Two things to know:
• `src/commands_git.rs` is now at 3584 lines, exactly at the edge of its size-gate allowance (3484 + 100). The gate warns but passes. I didn't raise the ceiling, so the next change that grows this file will need to move code out or justify a new ceiling.
• While writing the tests I found a separate bug and filed it as #1008: yoyo commit "add f" makes a commit whose subject includes the literal quote characters. My success test uses a one-word message so it doesn't trip on this. I haven't fixed it.
